1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:02,010
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:02,010 --> 00:00:03,270
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:04,110 --> 00:00:05,310
You are so scary.

4
00:00:06,080 --> 00:00:07,550
I haven't even said anything yet,

5
00:00:07,950 --> 00:00:09,480
so why are you glaring at me
so fiercely?

6
00:00:13,790 --> 00:00:16,250
Hold it in, Mi Mi. Jo Mi Mi.

7
00:00:16,790 --> 00:00:19,920
You gave birth to that burden.
You chose to have him.

8
00:00:21,030 --> 00:00:22,930
Who can you blame? Just hold it in.

9
00:00:23,430 --> 00:00:24,630
You're his mother.

10
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:28,030
They say if you're patient three times,
you can avoid committing murder.

11
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:35,670
Right now, I'm just glaring at you.

12
00:00:35,870 --> 00:00:38,510
But if you say one more word
and provoke your mother,

13
00:00:39,440 --> 00:00:42,510
I'll do more than glare at you.
I'll beat you to a pulp.

14
00:00:43,180 --> 00:00:44,180
Goodness.

15
00:00:44,920 --> 00:00:46,320
Su Ah's mom called me.

16
00:00:47,120 --> 00:00:48,650
She said you just met with her.

17
00:00:50,190 --> 00:00:52,460
- What did she say?
- She didn't say much.

18
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:54,730
She just asked how Su Ah was doing
and hung up.

19
00:00:56,230 --> 00:00:57,230
But Mom,

20
00:00:57,900 --> 00:01:00,830
why is Grandma suddenly
setting up a Yut board?

21
00:01:01,270 --> 00:01:02,630
It's been quiet for years.

22
00:01:03,540 --> 00:01:05,370
Isn't this the first time
we're playing...

23
00:01:05,370 --> 00:01:07,340
since that game we had
over you being stubborn about...

24
00:01:07,340 --> 00:01:08,370
getting Dae Chi his officetel?

25
00:01:08,740 --> 00:01:09,840
Wait a minute.

26
00:01:10,610 --> 00:01:13,510
Don't tell me
Dae Chi caused trouble too?

27
00:01:14,650 --> 00:01:16,580
And Grandma is trying
to find out about it?

28
00:01:18,750 --> 00:01:20,220
For someone so quick-witted,

29
00:01:20,220 --> 00:01:22,420
why did you mess up your marriage
so badly?

30
00:01:27,690 --> 00:01:30,900
Then I guess tonight,
I'm not the target of the Yut game.

31
00:01:32,060 --> 00:01:34,000
I was scared for nothing. Goodness.

32
00:01:34,770 --> 00:01:37,770
I thought Grandma
was trying to kick me out.

33
00:01:39,340 --> 00:01:40,340
But Mom,

34
00:01:41,070 --> 00:01:42,670
what kind of trouble
did Dae Chi cause?

35
00:01:42,910 --> 00:01:46,380
He is always so flawless
and lives such a perfect life.

36
00:01:47,910 --> 00:01:49,610
You are distracting me.

37
00:01:49,950 --> 00:01:51,380
You will find out
soon enough anyway.

38
00:01:51,450 --> 00:01:54,220
- Stop pestering your mother.
- Mom, I'm curious.

39
00:01:54,290 --> 00:01:55,450
What in the world happened?

40
00:01:57,560 --> 00:01:59,120
Why is this out here?

41
00:01:59,760 --> 00:02:02,230
If you took it out to eat,
you should put it back.

42
00:02:03,660 --> 00:02:04,730
What is that?

43
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:09,270
Mom.

44
00:02:11,040 --> 00:02:15,070
Mom, seriously.
You should be more careful.

45
00:02:16,010 --> 00:02:17,010
Are you okay?

46
00:02:17,580 --> 00:02:19,210
Do I look okay to you?

47
00:02:19,610 --> 00:02:20,610
Mom.

48
00:02:21,750 --> 00:02:22,780
What, you punk?

49
00:02:23,850 --> 00:02:24,850
You clean all of this up.

50
00:02:27,220 --> 00:02:28,220
Unbelievable.

51
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:32,620
Seriously. Where do I put this?

52
00:02:32,890 --> 00:02:34,030
Mom, where?

53
00:02:35,060 --> 00:02:37,360
In the refrigerator, where else?
You pain in the neck.

54
00:02:41,600 --> 00:02:43,870
Why is she getting mad at me
over radish kimchi?

55
00:02:50,740 --> 00:02:53,140
(Team Leader Kim Yeon Jung)

56
00:02:55,050 --> 00:02:59,280
- The customer is unavailable...
- Has the rumor already spread?

57
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:01,420
How can a single person
not be answering?

58
00:03:05,020 --> 00:03:06,820
These brats.

59
00:03:07,760 --> 00:03:10,860
I raised them all, and now they all
just crawl right back home.

60
00:03:11,460 --> 00:03:13,130
Look at these pants and socks.

61
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:15,270
They took them all off inside out.

62
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:16,470
Unbelievable.

63
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:19,940
Do they think
I'm their maid or something?

64
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:21,470
How can they be like this
their whole lives?

65
00:03:23,110 --> 00:03:25,040
They're all grown adults, too.

66
00:03:25,710 --> 00:03:27,110
Just my luck.

67
00:03:29,510 --> 00:03:30,520
Leave it.

68
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:32,980
I'll take it downstairs.

69
00:03:33,250 --> 00:03:36,290
You're all talk.
You guys are nothing but talk.

70
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:39,860
Just hurry up and come downstairs.
Don't keep Grandma waiting.

71
00:03:40,960 --> 00:03:41,960
Mom.

72
00:03:43,390 --> 00:03:44,630
It's definitely me today, right?

73
00:03:45,860 --> 00:03:46,860
Because of me, Grandma...

74
00:03:48,530 --> 00:03:50,700
Mom, you didn't tell her
everything, did you?

75
00:03:50,840 --> 00:03:52,070
If I had told her everything,

76
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:54,070
do you think Grandma
would be setting up a Yut board?

77
00:03:54,440 --> 00:03:55,670
Mom, what should I do?

78
00:03:56,040 --> 00:03:57,540
Grandma will collapse
if she finds out.

79
00:03:58,040 --> 00:04:00,780
Can't you just handle it
yourself this one time...

80
00:04:00,910 --> 00:04:02,450
and help me out?

81
00:04:03,580 --> 00:04:05,880
Just win. You just have to win.

82
00:04:06,220 --> 00:04:08,590
I'm saying this
because I'm not confident I can.

83
00:04:09,450 --> 00:04:11,860
Mom, please help me, okay?

84
00:04:12,520 --> 00:04:14,930
I really can't go downstairs.

85
00:04:15,190 --> 00:04:16,860
Since your grandma
already caught on,

86
00:04:16,930 --> 00:04:19,000
there's nothing I can do
to help you.

87
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:23,470
Why should I be the one to hear
that I raised my sons wrong?

88
00:04:25,070 --> 00:04:26,240
It's already happening anyway.

89
00:04:26,770 --> 00:04:27,770
Just come downstairs.

90
00:04:48,230 --> 00:04:50,260
Oh, Mom, give it to me.
I'll put it away.

91
00:04:50,330 --> 00:04:51,330
Okay.

92
00:04:51,930 --> 00:04:53,100
Goodness.

93
00:04:56,370 --> 00:04:57,370
All right.

94
00:04:58,440 --> 00:05:01,170
With more people,
laundry is a warzone.

95
00:05:01,670 --> 00:05:02,770
It's so overwhelming.

96
00:05:05,510 --> 00:05:09,050
I was definitely going
to do a load today,

97
00:05:09,380 --> 00:05:11,120
but Mrs. Choi made me do this...

98
00:05:15,950 --> 00:05:18,420
Grandma, here, have a seat.

99
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:19,920
Okay.

100
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:21,960
Why don't I see Dae Chi anywhere?

101
00:05:22,790 --> 00:05:24,200
He'll be down soon.

102
00:05:24,660 --> 00:05:25,660
Should I go get him?

103
00:05:27,500 --> 00:05:29,070
Thanks for finally
making it downstairs.

104
00:05:29,770 --> 00:05:31,970
I thought you were going to
come down tomorrow.

105
00:05:32,840 --> 00:05:34,570
Pour him a drink.

106
00:05:34,810 --> 00:05:37,180
- Three glasses for the latecomer.
- Yes.

107
00:05:47,790 --> 00:05:49,220
Just pour a little bit, will you?

108
00:05:54,090 --> 00:05:58,300
Grandma, what are the teams
for today's game?

109
00:05:58,930 --> 00:06:00,300
We have to pick teams, right?

110
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:02,600
Yes, the kids will be on that side,

111
00:06:02,670 --> 00:06:04,300
and your mom and Ri Ja
will be on my side.

112
00:06:05,670 --> 00:06:06,670
Su Ah.

113
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:10,410
My sweet girl,
could you hand me the yut?

114
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:11,610
Yes, Great-Grandma.

115
00:06:17,420 --> 00:06:20,520
You all know the rules,
but it's best three out of five.

116
00:06:20,850 --> 00:06:23,520
For each round, the losing team
must answer any question...

117
00:06:23,620 --> 00:06:26,060
the winning team asks
with absolute honesty.

118
00:06:26,560 --> 00:06:28,630
And to the team
that wins three times first,

119
00:06:28,690 --> 00:06:30,930
the losing team has to do
whatever they say.

120
00:06:31,830 --> 00:06:33,300
The teams that lose each round...

121
00:06:33,300 --> 00:06:35,800
will wash down their frustration
with makgeolli.

122
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:38,500
As always,
the referee will be Da Mi.

123
00:06:39,570 --> 00:06:40,710
Yes, Grandma.

124
00:06:40,970 --> 00:06:42,340
But Mrs. Choi,

125
00:06:43,010 --> 00:06:45,480
why is Da Mi the referee every time?

126
00:06:47,480 --> 00:06:50,080
I'm just curious.

127
00:06:51,050 --> 00:06:53,380
Because Da Mi is in charge
of the game board.

128
00:06:53,920 --> 00:06:56,850
Who else checks in on me
morning and night as much as Da Mi,

129
00:06:56,920 --> 00:06:58,520
other than President Jo?

130
00:06:59,090 --> 00:07:00,420
Step forward if there is anyone.

131
00:07:02,860 --> 00:07:05,430
Well, our youngest is
quite diligent.

132
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:06,900
Whether she has work or not.

133
00:07:07,170 --> 00:07:09,200
- Let's begin.
- But...

134
00:07:10,170 --> 00:07:12,400
let me ask you all just one thing.

135
00:07:12,940 --> 00:07:14,740
What is it, Grandma?

136
00:07:15,170 --> 00:07:19,340
Every time something happens,
do I have to set up a Yut board?

137
00:07:20,580 --> 00:07:23,310
We live under the same roof
and eat at the same table,

138
00:07:23,380 --> 00:07:25,420
so why am I always
the last to know...

139
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:27,120
when something serious happens
and needs attention?

140
00:07:27,120 --> 00:07:29,150
I'm very curious.

141
00:07:30,050 --> 00:07:33,290
Mi Mi, you are the head
of this household, so tell me.

142
00:07:35,130 --> 00:07:39,930
Well, you are getting older, Mother,
and you have high blood pressure,

143
00:07:40,330 --> 00:07:42,500
so we just worry about you.

144
00:07:42,630 --> 00:07:45,370
A few years ago, when you got...

145
00:07:45,740 --> 00:07:48,040
Dae Chi that officetel
without telling me so he could move out,

146
00:07:48,110 --> 00:07:49,540
I was very disappointed.

147
00:07:50,170 --> 00:07:52,180
But because I lost a game
of yut to you, Mi Mi,

148
00:07:52,240 --> 00:07:54,010
I did not say a word.

149
00:07:54,580 --> 00:07:55,580
Am I wrong?

150
00:07:57,320 --> 00:08:00,990
Right.
The frustrated one just has to win.

151
00:08:03,020 --> 00:08:04,620
That's right, Mrs. Choi.

152
00:08:04,990 --> 00:08:08,260
To be honest, we don't really know
the details of what happened either.

153
00:08:08,790 --> 00:08:11,900
Instead of making our arms hurt
by playing five rounds,

154
00:08:12,460 --> 00:08:14,170
why don't we just have the person...

155
00:08:14,230 --> 00:08:15,930
who caused trouble
confess voluntarily?

156
00:08:19,700 --> 00:08:21,270
So you want to play.

157
00:08:21,910 --> 00:08:22,940
I will handle...

158
00:08:23,570 --> 00:08:25,080
my own business.

159
00:08:25,610 --> 00:08:29,410
And just like Grandma said,
I just have to win.

160
00:08:31,680 --> 00:08:34,720
Hey, but why do we...

161
00:08:35,320 --> 00:08:37,520
have to be on his team
and win for him?

162
00:08:39,160 --> 00:08:40,630
Just stay still.

163
00:08:41,590 --> 00:08:42,590
Then...

164
00:08:43,160 --> 00:08:44,900
this side will go first.

165
00:08:45,660 --> 00:08:47,000
Mi Mi, you throw first.

166
00:08:47,670 --> 00:08:48,670
Yes, Mother.

167
00:08:56,840 --> 00:08:57,840
Geol...

168
00:08:58,610 --> 00:09:00,080
Then for our team,

169
00:09:00,510 --> 00:09:03,650
based on the porridge we ate,
I will throw first.

170
00:09:03,920 --> 00:09:05,320
Asura Balbalta.

171
00:09:05,680 --> 00:09:07,590
Asura Balbalta.

172
00:09:08,750 --> 00:09:09,890
- Geol, we got it.
- Geol, we caught...

173
00:09:09,950 --> 00:09:10,960
Geol, we caught them.

174
00:09:11,020 --> 00:09:12,760
- We caught them.
- We caught them!

175
00:09:12,820 --> 00:09:14,230
- We caught them!
- We caught them!

176
00:09:14,290 --> 00:09:18,130
- Catch them.
- Mi Mi, he must be really nervous.

177
00:09:18,660 --> 00:09:22,000
- But what exactly is going on?
- Keep your mouth shut.

178
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:24,370
I have nothing to say from now on.

179
00:09:25,640 --> 00:09:27,540
- Fine.
- Geol, stack them.

180
00:09:27,540 --> 00:09:29,610
- Should we stack them?
- Stack them.

181
00:09:29,670 --> 00:09:31,980
Keep throwing with that energy.

182
00:09:35,280 --> 00:09:36,450
Mo!

183
00:09:37,680 --> 00:09:41,590
This is amazing.
You throw a mo, Mrs. Choi.

184
00:09:45,860 --> 00:09:48,590
- Here.
- Goodness! It's a yut!

185
00:09:48,660 --> 00:09:51,200
- That is right.
- Wait, how did this happen again?

186
00:09:55,330 --> 00:09:57,000
We need to move quickly.

187
00:09:57,470 --> 00:10:00,070
This old woman gets sleepy
early in the evening.

188
00:10:00,140 --> 00:10:04,280
It really is amazing.
Mrs. Choi, what is your secret?

189
00:10:04,540 --> 00:10:06,740
Even a few years ago,
you took the lead right from the start.

190
00:10:07,880 --> 00:10:09,710
It is all about the momentum.

191
00:10:10,680 --> 00:10:12,320
My eldest grandson,
are you having fun?

192
00:10:12,850 --> 00:10:15,820
Mi Seon used to be so good
at throwing the yut.

193
00:10:16,020 --> 00:10:17,490
Are you having fun right now?

194
00:10:18,720 --> 00:10:19,860
Grandma.

195
00:10:20,730 --> 00:10:22,790
Why are you bringing up
Su Ah's mother...

196
00:10:23,330 --> 00:10:27,630
I'm just saying Mi Seon
was really good at throwing the yut.

197
00:10:29,630 --> 00:10:32,500
Mother.
Hurry and throw it one more time.

198
00:10:33,040 --> 00:10:34,040
Right.

199
00:10:35,670 --> 00:10:36,770
Gosh, it's a mo.

200
00:10:37,270 --> 00:10:39,480
Hey, Kang Da Mi, catch them!

201
00:10:39,540 --> 00:10:41,280
Catch them and stack them.

202
00:10:41,350 --> 00:10:42,580
If we stack them, we win.

203
00:10:43,180 --> 00:10:44,180
Here.

204
00:10:45,550 --> 00:10:47,150
- Gae! It's a gae!
- Gae.

205
00:10:47,220 --> 00:10:49,790
Okay, we caught them again.

206
00:10:51,990 --> 00:10:52,990
Again.

207
00:10:53,160 --> 00:10:56,130
Mi Mi, he's coming at us
as if his life depends on it.

208
00:10:57,130 --> 00:10:58,460
- Geol.
- Geol.

209
00:10:58,530 --> 00:11:02,330
Mrs. Choi, what should we do?
It's my turn.

210
00:11:02,630 --> 00:11:03,900
What do you mean?

211
00:11:03,970 --> 00:11:06,140
Put your heart and soul into it
as you throw.

212
00:11:08,010 --> 00:11:09,010
All right.

213
00:11:09,510 --> 00:11:11,010
I'm throwing.

214
00:11:11,580 --> 00:11:12,610
Throw it gently.

215
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:14,080
Okay.

216
00:11:21,250 --> 00:11:22,290
Goodness!

217
00:11:22,290 --> 00:11:25,490
I threw a yut, Mrs. Choi.

218
00:11:26,520 --> 00:11:28,330
How marvelous.

219
00:11:28,690 --> 00:11:30,060
They say even a good-for-nothing
can come in handy.

220
00:11:30,130 --> 00:11:31,730
Looks like we've got one
right here at home.

221
00:11:32,060 --> 00:11:34,570
Hurry up and throw again.
Just keep on throwing.

222
00:11:35,770 --> 00:11:38,570
Read the room.
Why are you throwing a yut too?

223
00:11:39,300 --> 00:11:40,910
I said to take it easy.

224
00:11:42,640 --> 00:11:43,640
Dae Chi.

225
00:11:45,340 --> 00:11:46,410
Yes, Grandma.

226
00:11:46,910 --> 00:11:48,250
Do you have anything to say?

227
00:11:51,320 --> 00:11:53,550
- I don't.
- Is that so?

228
00:11:54,050 --> 00:11:56,490
He says he does not.
What are you doing?

229
00:11:56,650 --> 00:11:59,360
Hurry up and throw it
so we can go to sleep.

230
00:12:11,440 --> 00:12:14,140
What is it? What did she get?

231
00:12:14,710 --> 00:12:17,980
- That's a do, right?
- No. It's a back do.

232
00:12:19,040 --> 00:12:20,040
That's it.

233
00:12:20,780 --> 00:12:21,850
The game is over.

234
00:12:22,780 --> 00:12:24,480
Since we caught you with a back do,

235
00:12:25,080 --> 00:12:26,480
we get to take ours out first.

236
00:12:27,850 --> 00:12:30,860
(Finish)

237
00:12:31,290 --> 00:12:32,320
We won.

238
00:12:33,290 --> 00:12:35,390
No, wait a minute, Grandma.

239
00:12:36,660 --> 00:12:38,900
How did the game end up like this?

240
00:12:39,660 --> 00:12:42,330
Dae Chi, what kind of trouble
did you get into?

241
00:12:43,370 --> 00:12:44,400
Is it a woman?

242
00:12:45,400 --> 00:12:46,470
Or money?

243
00:12:50,770 --> 00:12:53,480
A grown man shouldn't act so petty.

244
00:12:54,510 --> 00:12:55,850
Just spit it out.

245
00:12:59,480 --> 00:13:02,490
Hey. It's all over.

246
00:13:02,950 --> 00:13:05,090
Just come clean and tell her.

247
00:13:06,520 --> 00:13:09,590
Drinking makgeolli after a long time
is making me tired and sleepy.

248
00:13:10,130 --> 00:13:12,460
I don't think it's a woman issue.

249
00:13:13,130 --> 00:13:14,900
What on earth is it?

250
00:13:18,140 --> 00:13:20,270
Well, you see...

251
00:13:21,410 --> 00:13:24,640
- I...
- This is so frustrating.

252
00:13:25,180 --> 00:13:27,180
Just tell her already.

253
00:13:27,240 --> 00:13:29,710
Mom is so upset that
she keeps drinking makgeolli.

254
00:13:32,420 --> 00:13:33,750
The thing is, Mother.

255
00:13:36,250 --> 00:13:37,920
I'm so sorry...

256
00:13:38,990 --> 00:13:39,990
to have to tell you this,

257
00:13:40,060 --> 00:13:41,790
and I'm too ashamed
to even look at you.

258
00:13:42,990 --> 00:13:44,030
What?

259
00:13:44,500 --> 00:13:46,560
Are you trying to cover
for your kid again?

260
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:48,670
You might as well have been
a blanket seller.

261
00:13:51,100 --> 00:13:53,770
What is your mouth for? Speak.

262
00:13:56,370 --> 00:13:57,410
He came home...

263
00:13:58,480 --> 00:14:01,380
with a massive amount of debt.

264
00:14:02,850 --> 00:14:03,850
Mom!

265
00:14:04,110 --> 00:14:05,450
If it's massive,

266
00:14:06,380 --> 00:14:07,450
how much?

267
00:14:09,120 --> 00:14:10,120
Hey,

268
00:14:10,790 --> 00:14:13,260
you useless brat. You tell her.

269
00:14:13,860 --> 00:14:15,130
I said, tell her.

270
00:14:15,690 --> 00:14:18,700
Why can you not say it?
Do you think Grandma will collapse?

271
00:14:20,060 --> 00:14:21,070
Hey!

272
00:14:21,970 --> 00:14:24,200
Don't you know what kind of person
your grandma is?

273
00:14:24,670 --> 00:14:27,240
She has been through
all the joys and sorrows...

274
00:14:27,300 --> 00:14:29,410
and overcome every hurdle in life.

275
00:14:31,980 --> 00:14:32,980
Mom.

276
00:14:33,740 --> 00:14:34,810
Come on!

277
00:14:36,010 --> 00:14:38,250
Grandma, I think
we should put Mom to bed.

278
00:14:38,350 --> 00:14:39,480
No, leave her be.

279
00:14:40,950 --> 00:14:44,590
Go on, finish what you were saying.
Hurry up.

280
00:14:48,260 --> 00:14:49,330
That brat...

281
00:14:50,360 --> 00:14:51,400
got into debt...

282
00:14:51,960 --> 00:14:55,300
He followed a senior from work
and invested in something.

283
00:14:56,130 --> 00:14:57,470
The debt, Mother...

284
00:14:59,870 --> 00:15:04,340
It's 1,130,000 dollars.

285
00:15:07,910 --> 00:15:10,810
- Mom.
- How much?

286
00:15:10,810 --> 00:15:12,550
It's 1,100,000 dollars?

287
00:15:14,120 --> 00:15:15,120
Hey.

288
00:15:15,850 --> 00:15:18,220
I heard that wrong, right?

289
00:15:19,290 --> 00:15:20,390
Not 100,000 dollars,

290
00:15:20,990 --> 00:15:22,190
not 200,000 dollars...

291
00:15:23,430 --> 00:15:25,500
How much was it again?

292
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:27,970
It's 1,100,000 dollars?

293
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:32,600
It's 1,130,000 dollars.

294
00:15:35,510 --> 00:15:37,470
Grandma, are you okay?

295
00:15:38,040 --> 00:15:40,180
Should I get you a calming pill?

296
00:15:40,780 --> 00:15:42,050
I'm fine.

297
00:15:44,350 --> 00:15:45,920
I'm perfectly fine.

298
00:15:50,120 --> 00:15:51,920
- Mrs. Choi.
- Grandma.

299
00:15:57,360 --> 00:15:58,560
It's 1,100,000 dollars...

300
00:15:59,660 --> 00:16:01,270
A debt of 1,100,000 dollars...

301
00:16:16,580 --> 00:16:17,580
Mom.

302
00:16:22,350 --> 00:16:23,450
My gosh.

303
00:16:29,960 --> 00:16:31,330
Is it warmed up enough?

304
00:16:31,760 --> 00:16:32,800
Yes, ma'am.

305
00:16:33,360 --> 00:16:34,400
Let me see.

306
00:16:36,270 --> 00:16:38,370
It's perfect. I told you
to pay special attention...

307
00:16:38,440 --> 00:16:39,870
to the deer antlers.

308
00:16:39,940 --> 00:16:42,240
Just the smell of it tells me
it will be good for his health.

309
00:16:42,470 --> 00:16:43,870
I will bring it up to him.

310
00:16:44,710 --> 00:16:47,180
Wait. I will take it up.

311
00:16:55,120 --> 00:16:56,690
My eldest grandson.

312
00:16:59,690 --> 00:17:03,690
If you run for this long,
your injured leg will hurt.

313
00:17:04,400 --> 00:17:06,960
Are you sure it is okay
to run every morning?

314
00:17:08,330 --> 00:17:10,370
It's fine because I run slowly,
Grandma.

315
00:17:11,240 --> 00:17:14,910
Even in the US,
you ran every single morning?

316
00:17:16,010 --> 00:17:20,640
Yes, I ran consistently every day.
That's really important.

317
00:17:20,780 --> 00:17:23,880
But now, for the most part,
I live without feeling any pain.

318
00:17:24,050 --> 00:17:25,850
I'm fine,
so don't worry too much, Grandma.

319
00:17:27,120 --> 00:17:31,560
My admirable Seung Yun.
My eldest grandson.

320
00:17:35,830 --> 00:17:36,830
Yes.

321
00:17:38,330 --> 00:17:41,670
- Mother, you were up here.
- Yes.

322
00:17:43,030 --> 00:17:45,100
Have you adjusted
to the time difference?

323
00:17:45,600 --> 00:17:46,740
How are you feeling?

324
00:17:47,740 --> 00:17:49,210
I'm fine.

325
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:53,110
- What is this?
- This is herbal medicine...

326
00:17:53,110 --> 00:17:54,680
I had prepared for you.

327
00:17:54,880 --> 00:17:56,480
I'll make sure you have it
every morning and night,

328
00:17:56,680 --> 00:17:58,480
so don't skip it
and keep drinking it for a while.

329
00:18:03,220 --> 00:18:04,220
What are you doing?

330
00:18:04,350 --> 00:18:06,060
You should drink it quickly
before it gets cold.

331
00:18:07,220 --> 00:18:09,760
Yes, thank you. I will enjoy this.

332
00:18:10,190 --> 00:18:12,030
Stop it, Seung Yun.

333
00:18:13,130 --> 00:18:15,600
- What's wrong, Grandma?
- Give that to me.

334
00:18:18,940 --> 00:18:20,740
I'm going to drink it.

335
00:18:20,940 --> 00:18:22,840
Were you going to drink
this delicious thing...

336
00:18:22,840 --> 00:18:24,340
all by yourself without me?

337
00:18:24,880 --> 00:18:26,180
I'm going to drink it first.

338
00:18:27,880 --> 00:18:28,880
Grandma.

339
00:18:29,280 --> 00:18:32,820
Mother, that's medicine
I got made for Seung Yun.

340
00:18:35,420 --> 00:18:38,290
What did you put in this
to make it so bitter, sister?

341
00:18:39,420 --> 00:18:40,560
Give me candy.

342
00:18:41,930 --> 00:18:43,590
Please give me some candy.

343
00:18:44,730 --> 00:18:46,500
- Grandma, who am I?
- What?

344
00:18:46,530 --> 00:18:47,900
Do you recognize me?

345
00:18:50,030 --> 00:18:51,470
Don't be shaken, Seung Yun.

346
00:18:51,640 --> 00:18:55,170
She kept a clear mind for a few days
because you came back.

347
00:18:56,670 --> 00:18:58,480
It's okay, so don't be surprised.

348
00:19:22,700 --> 00:19:23,970
Did you sleep well, Mother?

349
00:19:25,240 --> 00:19:26,240
Yes.

350
00:19:26,370 --> 00:19:28,070
Are you coming down
from seeing Seung Yun?

351
00:19:28,770 --> 00:19:30,910
Would you like me to help you
wash up today?

352
00:19:31,580 --> 00:19:36,250
You are talking nonsense.
I washed up a long time ago.

353
00:19:37,780 --> 00:19:39,220
Do the company work...

354
00:19:39,580 --> 00:19:41,620
exactly as I told you.

355
00:19:42,390 --> 00:19:44,590
I will be checking thoroughly.

356
00:19:45,360 --> 00:19:47,460
Yes, Mother.
I have already ordered them...

357
00:19:47,460 --> 00:19:49,790
to process it
as quickly as possible.

358
00:19:50,230 --> 00:19:51,330
I will report to you separately.

359
00:20:05,380 --> 00:20:07,210
Did Mother go into her room alone?

360
00:20:07,480 --> 00:20:09,250
Yes, just now. Why?

361
00:20:10,810 --> 00:20:11,980
She does not seem lucid.

362
00:20:12,650 --> 00:20:13,850
Did Seung Yun see her too?

363
00:20:14,520 --> 00:20:17,520
Yes. He seemed a bit shocked.

364
00:20:18,260 --> 00:20:20,590
Well, she took the bowl
of herbal medicine...

365
00:20:20,590 --> 00:20:21,930
that I brought for Seung Yun...

366
00:20:22,430 --> 00:20:25,200
and drank it all at once
like a child, honey.

367
00:20:25,860 --> 00:20:28,270
Goodness.
She had been fine for a few days.

368
00:20:29,330 --> 00:20:32,270
But when she was talking
to me just now,

369
00:20:32,600 --> 00:20:34,000
she seemed perfectly fine.

370
00:20:35,370 --> 00:20:37,770
It's not like
flipping a light switch on and off.

371
00:20:37,770 --> 00:20:38,810
Goodness.

372
00:20:39,540 --> 00:20:43,480
Don't worry too much.
I will try calling Dr. Ju.

373
00:20:52,690 --> 00:20:56,630
Who knows if that medicine
is real or not?

374
00:21:00,630 --> 00:21:03,800
I cannot watch anything
with peace of mind anymore.

375
00:21:05,040 --> 00:21:07,440
Why is my heart like this?

376
00:21:20,880 --> 00:21:23,920
(Dr. Ju)

377
00:21:27,520 --> 00:21:29,890
Yes, this is Ju Kyung Ho. Go ahead.

378
00:21:30,560 --> 00:21:32,660
Yes, I'm sorry to call
so early in the morning, Dr. Ju.

379
00:21:32,860 --> 00:21:35,630
Not at all. Did something happen
to the Madam Chairwoman?

380
00:21:36,070 --> 00:21:39,140
Well, I'm calling about my mother.

381
00:21:39,470 --> 00:21:40,500
Is it a good time to talk?

382
00:21:41,040 --> 00:21:42,740
Yes, go ahead.

383
00:21:44,210 --> 00:21:47,310
What is this? It is about my mother,
so why is he so calm?

384
00:21:48,250 --> 00:21:49,250
Hello?

385
00:21:50,510 --> 00:21:51,650
Yes.

386
00:21:52,320 --> 00:21:53,520
The thing is,

387
00:21:53,720 --> 00:21:56,920
my mother's mind
takes a turn for the worse,

388
00:21:57,250 --> 00:22:00,520
but then suddenly, she becomes lucid again
as if nothing happened.

389
00:22:01,220 --> 00:22:03,230
She just did that a moment ago.

390
00:22:03,430 --> 00:22:06,000
Actually, my wife and I think...

391
00:22:06,330 --> 00:22:07,560
we should take her
to a university hospital...

392
00:22:07,560 --> 00:22:11,030
as early as tomorrow
to get her examined.

393
00:22:12,300 --> 00:22:13,370
Hello?

394
00:22:13,940 --> 00:22:14,940
Dr. Ju?

395
00:22:16,340 --> 00:22:17,410
Are you listening?

396
00:22:19,210 --> 00:22:20,380
Yes, I'm listening.

397
00:22:22,480 --> 00:22:27,180
Anyway, I honestly want to hear
your opinion as well.

398
00:22:27,720 --> 00:22:30,950
I would like to meet with you.
Can you come to the office?

399
00:22:31,820 --> 00:22:32,820
Yes, understood.

400
00:22:33,160 --> 00:22:35,930
If you text me a convenient time,
I will come see you.

401
00:22:36,190 --> 00:22:38,660
Yes, I will contact you
through my secretary then.

402
00:22:42,670 --> 00:22:45,400
What is with him?
Does he have a stick up his butt?

403
00:22:47,100 --> 00:22:48,570
Why is he so stiff?

404
00:23:17,730 --> 00:23:19,170
It's about time he showed up.

405
00:23:20,700 --> 00:23:23,040
Hello. Can I help you with anything?

406
00:23:27,510 --> 00:23:28,510
I'm fine.

407
00:23:30,310 --> 00:23:31,310
Team Leader Cha?

408
00:23:31,950 --> 00:23:33,050
Fancy seeing you here.

409
00:23:33,650 --> 00:23:35,120
Assistant Manager Kang,
what brings you here?

410
00:23:35,790 --> 00:23:38,320
I came to the gym to work out,
what else?

411
00:23:38,860 --> 00:23:40,060
Since when have you
been coming here?

412
00:23:40,360 --> 00:23:41,360
Today's my first day.

413
00:23:41,660 --> 00:23:42,690
I see.

414
00:23:42,830 --> 00:23:45,130
If I had known you came here,
Team Leader Cha,

415
00:23:45,460 --> 00:23:47,260
I would have registered sooner.

416
00:23:47,660 --> 00:23:50,570
Working out together before work
is absolutely perfect. Right?

417
00:23:52,100 --> 00:23:55,010
Since I just started,
I have a lot of questions too.

418
00:23:55,270 --> 00:23:56,910
I prefer to work out alone.

419
00:23:57,710 --> 00:24:00,680
Team Leader Cha.
It's not like we are strangers.

420
00:24:00,740 --> 00:24:02,680
- Kang Ye Ri.
- Yes?

421
00:24:02,980 --> 00:24:04,110
Let's keep work...

422
00:24:04,110 --> 00:24:05,620
and our personal lives separate,
even outside the office.

423
00:24:06,280 --> 00:24:07,520
You are not a new employee,
honestly.

424
00:24:27,100 --> 00:24:28,170
Work and personal lives?

425
00:24:28,710 --> 00:24:29,840
What a joke.

426
00:24:33,180 --> 00:24:34,610
Does he think I'll give up
because of this?

427
00:24:38,380 --> 00:24:39,380
What?

428
00:24:42,050 --> 00:24:43,950
I thought we could at least
go to work together.

429
00:25:00,340 --> 00:25:02,510
He has completely lost his mind.

430
00:25:19,620 --> 00:25:20,860
Are you the only one
living in this house?

431
00:25:21,590 --> 00:25:23,030
What's wrong now, Mom?

432
00:25:24,830 --> 00:25:26,460
I would've cleaned it up.

433
00:25:26,660 --> 00:25:28,600
You didn't have to bring it here.

434
00:25:28,830 --> 00:25:30,730
You should have cleaned it up
right after you drank it.

435
00:25:31,470 --> 00:25:33,200
Don't you think about
how upset Grandma would be...

436
00:25:33,200 --> 00:25:34,270
if she saw this?

437
00:25:34,970 --> 00:25:35,970
What about you, Mom?

438
00:25:37,010 --> 00:25:39,610
For someone who worries so much
about Grandma's health,

439
00:25:39,710 --> 00:25:41,340
what were you thinking
playing yut yesterday...

440
00:25:41,410 --> 00:25:43,980
when you exposed all of my debt
like that?

441
00:25:45,150 --> 00:25:46,620
You were even drunk.

442
00:25:48,050 --> 00:25:49,490
It was so embarrassing.

443
00:25:50,790 --> 00:25:54,290
How am I supposed to face Grandma
and the rest of the family now?

444
00:25:54,720 --> 00:25:56,530
Is your pride still
that important to you?

445
00:25:57,530 --> 00:25:58,700
Are you the only one with pride?

446
00:25:59,500 --> 00:26:02,200
I spend all day
working with your Grandma,

447
00:26:02,270 --> 00:26:04,000
and I can barely even breathe.

448
00:26:05,400 --> 00:26:07,900
If you want to soothe your stomach
with that rotten water so badly,

449
00:26:08,040 --> 00:26:09,110
go out and buy your own drinks.

450
00:26:10,210 --> 00:26:12,380
Oh, right. You don't have any money.

451
00:26:13,540 --> 00:26:15,280
Then drink without anyone knowing...

452
00:26:15,980 --> 00:26:18,950
and clean up the empty bottles
quietly right where you drank them.

453
00:26:19,280 --> 00:26:20,350
Got it?

454
00:26:55,120 --> 00:26:56,120
Honey.

455
00:26:57,850 --> 00:26:58,860
That's not it.

456
00:26:59,320 --> 00:27:00,520
What are you talking about?

457
00:27:01,060 --> 00:27:02,130
You said it was on the first floor.

458
00:27:02,260 --> 00:27:03,530
No, that's the second floor.

459
00:27:04,260 --> 00:27:06,800
Apartment 101 down there
is our place.

460
00:27:16,310 --> 00:27:18,710
What? This is a semi-basement.

461
00:27:20,710 --> 00:27:22,050
Semi-basement?

462
00:27:22,380 --> 00:27:25,650
This is listed as the first floor
on the address.

463
00:27:25,950 --> 00:27:27,420
I checked it very carefully.

464
00:27:27,480 --> 00:27:31,120
- It gets good sunlight here, too.
- Are you kidding me right now?

465
00:27:32,590 --> 00:27:34,860
Did you eat something invigorating
all by yourself?

466
00:27:35,360 --> 00:27:36,760
Why are you being so loud?

467
00:27:39,830 --> 00:27:41,630
What are you doing right now?

468
00:27:42,170 --> 00:27:43,300
Hurry up and get up.

469
00:27:44,500 --> 00:27:47,100
I can't live in a house like this,
so look for another place right now.

470
00:27:47,270 --> 00:27:48,940
I'm not moving
a single step from here.

471
00:27:50,610 --> 00:27:51,640
This is unbelievable, really.

472
00:27:52,280 --> 00:27:55,810
Even if my life has hit rock bottom
since I met you,

473
00:27:56,310 --> 00:27:57,350
this is just not right.

474
00:28:09,690 --> 00:28:11,660
(Mission: Mompossible)

475
00:28:11,760 --> 00:28:13,260
Don't you know Ye Ri
is discussing marriage...

476
00:28:13,260 --> 00:28:14,660
with the son of her company's CEO?

477
00:28:14,930 --> 00:28:16,270
How can you make a girl...

478
00:28:16,270 --> 00:28:17,800
who might marry someone
who could be Hwanggeum Apparel's CEO...

479
00:28:17,870 --> 00:28:18,970
live in a place like this?

480
00:28:19,100 --> 00:28:21,570
- Does that even make sense?
- It's been so long...

481
00:28:21,640 --> 00:28:23,310
since I had to nag so much
about a design.

482
00:28:23,710 --> 00:28:25,480
How could Dae Chi do this to me?

483
00:28:25,640 --> 00:28:26,980
Did he really mean that?

484
00:28:29,280 --> 00:28:31,250
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
